From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: llcc: sm8350: match the slice flags to the downstream table

The sm8350 slice table was converted from the downstream lahaina table
(llcc-lahaina.c, SCT_ENTRY(uid, sid, mc, p, fs, bway, rway, cmod, ptw, dca,
wse, rp, a)) with the last three columns shifted: activate_on_init took the
retain_on_pc column, write_scid_en the activate_on_init column and
retain_on_pc the write_scid_en column. As a result 15 slices (video,
modem, compute, display, audio HW, CVP, the TCM slice APTCM, ...) are
activated at probe and never released, while downstream activates only
CPUSS, MMUHWT, WRCACHE and CPUHWT and keeps the ways of almost every slice
retained over power collapse. On the ROG Phone 5 the LLCC/DDR subsystem
never idles in s2idle (DDR stays at its lowest clock plan without entering
any DDR low-power mode, and the AOP names only DDR_AUX as the CX collapse
blocker).

Restore the downstream write_scid_en / retain_on_pc / activate_on_init
values for every sm8350 slice. The other fields already match.

